 "notes": "Headline limit: 90% CL (Delta chi^2 = 1.64, eq. 3.4) exclusion on dark-photon kinetic mixing epsilon from Hinode XRT dark (calibration) images with radial & spectral information and data-driven background subtraction -- the 'HINODE: darks (optimistic)' curve of figure 8 (solid purple in figure 5). Extracted from the vector paths of figures/figure_8.pdf in the e-print; axis calibration cross-checked against Table 1 (epsilon ~ 1e-9 at m = 1 eV, kink mass ~3e-2 eV, both reproduced). Curve clipped at epsilon = 1 on both the low-mass slope-(-2) tail and the high-mass kinematic cutoff near 2.3 keV; wiggles at 0.03-0.25 eV are the resonant-conversion structure in the plot. The paper also derives a second, complementary limit from a 2012 solar-eclipse image ('HINODE: eclipse'), stronger than the darks limit only below ~1 meV; not included here. Helioscope (solar flux) limit, no dark-matter density assumption.",
